import object_detector

def get_closest_robot():
    result = object_detector.execute(image='path/to/image.png', languages=['en', 'de'], save_object=True, saved_image_path='detected_objects')
    detected_objects = result[0]
    detected_objects_image_paths = [result[0].saved_image_path for _ in detected_objects]

    if len(detected_objects) == 0:
        nearest_text_found = letter_detector.execute(image='path/to/image.png')
        return nearest_text_found[0].bbox, nearest_text_found[0].letter, nearest_text_found[0].score

    minimal_distance = detected_objects[0]['bbox'][0] + 5  # Keep 5 pixels distance as a safety buffer

    return [bbox for bbox in detected_objects if bbox[0][1] < minimal_distance]
```

Please replace `'path/to/image.png'` with the actual path of your image.

Note: This solution requires installing the `object_detector` and `letter_detector` Python packages through pip or conda. These packages will be installed if pturned available on the code execution host.

